# ---------------------------------------------------------------- to raise a family that holds together (W, cycle s4)

== the whole family round one table
tier: life event
aim: to raise a family that holds together
aim_role: spark
stages: young_adult adult mature
age: 24-64
per_year: 0 0 .3 .4 .3 0
tone: mixed
life: family, home
horizon: week
roles: parent, sibling, partner, child, grandparent
earth: a Sunday lunch at one's own table, with every branch of the family asked
tribal: a feast at one's own hearth, with every branch of the family called in
magic: a feast-day supper in one's own hall, with every branch of the household summoned
scene: {N} has asked the whole family for Sunday lunch, the first time at {Ns} own table, and {sibling} and {parent} have not spoken since spring.
scene W: {N} has set a place for everyone, even the ones who said they might not come.
scene U: {N} has worked out who sits where, which subjects to steer round, and when to bring out the pudding.
scene B: This is {Ns} table now, and {N} wants everyone to see the family is run from here.
scene R: {N} has cooked far too much and turned the music up, and wants the house loud.
scene G: The smell of the old family dish fills the hall, the one everyone grew up on.
- W | set a place for everyone, and ring each of them the night before | v: tradition, benevolence | dream: test | foot: means time-.04 | chance: 72
- U | seat the two who have fallen out at opposite ends of the table | v: security | foot: lesson small plans keep the peace | chance: 80
- B | keep the best seats for those who came last time, and let the others notice | v: power | foot: door made an enemy | chance: 70
- R | throw the doors open and ask the neighbours in too, the more the better | v: hedonism, benevolence | foot: person neighbour | chance: 75
- G | cook the old family dish the way it was always cooked, from memory | v: tradition | foot: mark learned a skill | chance: 82
- W>G | ask the two who have fallen out to lay the table together | v: benevolence, conformity | dream: seal | foot: means ties+.06 | chance: 55
- U>W | start a family calendar so that every birthday gets a call | v: conformity, benevolence | foot: door kept your word | chance: 78
- B>U | find out quietly what the row was really about before anyone arrives | v: power, security | foot: door kept it hidden | chance: 68
- R>B | tell the two of them straight that this lunch is happening, like it or not | v: power, self-direction | foot: means ties-.04 | chance: 60
- G>R | call off the lunch and take whoever wants to come out to the park | v: hedonism, benevolence | dream: drop | foot: lesson family needs no table | chance: 85
works: By the pudding, {sibling} and {parent} are passing each other the jug, and nobody mentions the spring.
works: The table is too small and the chairs do not match, and {N} has never been happier to wash up.
fails: {parent} leaves before the main course, and the front door bangs.
fails: Half the chairs stay empty, and {N} eats the leftovers for a week.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- to keep the peace in the street (W, cycle s3)

== two neighbours squaring up on the pavement
tier: life event
aim: to keep the peace in the street
aim_role: spark
stages: young_adult adult mature elder
age: 16-85
per_year: 0 0 .3 .4 .4 .3
tone: trouble
life: neighbours, community
horizon: moment
roles: neighbours, friend, rival
earth: two neighbours shouting over a parking space, and the whole street coming out to watch
tribal: two families of the camp shouting over a fishing place, and the whole camp coming out to watch
magic: two shopkeepers in the lane below the tower shouting over a market pitch, and the lane coming out to watch
scene: It is a warm evening, and two neighbours are nose to nose over a parking space, voices rising, while curtains twitch the length of the street.
scene W: Someone has to step in before a fist is thrown, and {N} is already crossing the road.
scene U: {N} has seen this coming for weeks: the van, the bins, the hedge, and now the parking space.
scene B: Both men owe {N} a favour, and a favour is a handle.
scene R: {Ns} heart is pounding; the shouting is like a spark on dry grass.
scene G: This street has been {Ns} home for years, and {N} hates to see it torn.
- W | walk between the two of them and ask, calmly, for five minutes of quiet | v: security, benevolence | dream: test | foot: person neighbour | chance: 60
- U | hear each side out in turn, and note what each one actually wants | v: universalism | foot: lesson every row has two stories | chance: 70
- B | warn them both that the police will be called, and mean it | v: power, security | foot: place prot.watch | chance: 72
- R | shout louder than either of them until both stop and stare | v: stimulation | foot: person rival | chance: 55
- G | bring out chairs and a pot of tea, and sit everyone down on the wall | v: benevolence | foot: means ties+.05 | chance: 68
- W>R | step in hard and fast, and split them up before it turns ugly | v: security | dream: test | foot: door helped someone in need | chance: 58
- U>G | propose a rota for the space, drawn up by the whole street together | v: universalism, conformity | foot: place rule.counsel | chance: 62
- B>W | offer to settle it, so long as both agree to abide by the ruling | v: power, conformity | foot: door made an enemy | chance: 54
- R>U | film the whole row and play it back to them once they calm down | v: stimulation, self-direction | foot: lesson a mirror cools a temper | chance: 50
- G>B | stay out of it, draw the curtains, and leave them to it | v: security | dream: drop | foot: means ties-.04 | chance: 90
works: The shouting stops, and by the weekend the two of them are nodding to each other over the bins.
works: The street goes back indoors, and someone leaves a cake on {Ns} step the next morning.
fails: A punch is thrown after all, and a police car sits outside till midnight.
fails: Both neighbours turn on {N} for interfering, and the row moves to the residents' meeting.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- to see justice done (W, cycle s2)

== the evening at the free advice desk
tier: life event
aim: to see justice done
aim_role: spark
stages: young_adult adult mature
age: 18-65
per_year: 0 0 .4 .4 .3 0
tone: mixed
life: work, law, community
horizon: months
roles: mentor, colleague, a tenant, a landlord
earth: an evening at the free legal advice desk, and an old tenant who has been wrongly locked out
tribal: an evening at the elders' fire, and an old fisher wrongly turned off the family's fishing place
magic: an evening at the guild's petition table, and an old lodger wrongly turned out of his rooms
scene: The free advice desk opens at six, and {Ns} first case is an old man with a carrier bag full of letters: his landlord has changed the locks.
scene W: The law says plainly that a tenant cannot be put out like this, and {N} means to see the law kept.
scene U: Somewhere in the bag of letters is the date that wins the case, and {N} means to find it.
scene B: The landlord owns half the street, and beating him would make {Ns} name.
scene R: {N} is furious on the old man's behalf and wants to march round to the landlord tonight.
scene G: The old man has lived in that flat for forty years, and his whole life is behind that locked door.
- W | take the case properly: file the papers and see it through to the hearing | v: universalism, conformity | dream: test | foot: door kept your word | chance: 60
- U | sort the letters by date until the one that proves it turns up | v: achievement | foot: mark learned a skill | chance: 75
- B | ring the landlord and drop a hint about the local paper | v: power | foot: person rival | chance: 55
- R | go round with the old man that night and demand the keys back | v: stimulation, benevolence | foot: mark took a wild risk | chance: 45
- G | find him a bed for the night first, and leave the law till morning | v: benevolence | foot: mark helped someone in need | chance: 85
- W>B | ask the senior lawyer for the lead on the case, under their eye | v: achievement | dream: test | foot: person mentor | chance: 58
- U>R | stay late every night that week and build the case from nothing | v: achievement, stimulation | foot: means time-.06 | chance: 70
- B>G | get the landlord to pay for a hotel quietly, in return for no fuss | v: security, power | foot: door turned down a chance | chance: 66
- R>W | stand up at the residents' meeting and tell the whole street what happened | v: universalism | foot: place rule.voice | chance: 62
- G>U | pass him to a housing lawyer, and walk him to the office door | v: benevolence | dream: drop | foot: person colleague | chance: 80
works: The locks are changed back within the fortnight, and the old man brings a tin of biscuits to the desk every week after.
works: The hearing is short, the ruling is plain, and {N} walks out into the rain grinning.
fails: The landlord's lawyer finds a missed date, and the case falls apart on a technicality.
fails: The old man gives up and moves in with his daughter before the hearing comes.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- to keep one promise for life (W, cycle s1)

== the year the promise gets heavy
tier: life event
aim: to keep one promise for life
aim_role: spark
stages: young_adult adult mature elder
age: 18-90
per_year: 0 0 .3 .3 .3 .3
needs: partner
tone: mixed
life: love, partner
horizon: months
roles: partner, friend, parent
earth: a partner out of work, and the long winter evenings gone quiet
tribal: a partner hurt in the hunt, and a long winter at the fire begun
magic: a partner turned away from the tower's service, and a long winter in the rooms begun
scene: {partner} has lost the job, and the evenings have gone quiet. {N} once promised "in good times and in bad", and these are the bad ones.
scene W: {N} meant every word of that promise, and a promise means most when it costs something.
scene U: {N} lies awake working out what {partner} actually needs, and how much of it is hurt pride.
scene B: {N} has an offer of work in another city, the kind that comes once.
scene R: {N} misses the laughing, the dancing, the old {partner}, and is tired of this one.
scene G: The house feels like a burrow in winter, and {N} wants to keep it warm until spring.
- W | stay close, and say every day that this will pass | v: benevolence, tradition | dream: test | foot: door kept your word | chance: 70
- U | sit down together and plan the year line by line, so nothing comes as a shock | v: security | foot: lesson a plan halves a fear | chance: 72
- B | take the job in the other city, and come home at weekends | v: achievement | foot: means money+.06 | chance: 68
- R | book a weekend away on a whim, to shake the gloom off both of them | v: hedonism, stimulation | foot: means money-.04 | chance: 75
- G | keep the house warm and the meals coming, and let the winter pass | v: benevolence, security | foot: lesson patience is a kind of love | chance: 80
- W>U | write the old promise out again by hand and leave it on the pillow | v: tradition, benevolence | dream: seal | foot: mark kept your word | chance: 76
- U>B | help rewrite the CV and rehearse every interview together | v: achievement | foot: means time-.05 | chance: 70
- B>R | push the two of them back out to see the old friends, ready or not | v: stimulation | foot: person friend | chance: 60
- R>G | take on an allotment together, and dig the gloom out | v: hedonism, universalism (nature) | foot: place prod.land | chance: 70
- G>W | ask both families round, and let them carry some of the weight | v: tradition, benevolence | foot: means ties+.05 | chance: 74
works: By spring {partner} is laughing again, and the promise feels stronger for the bending.
works: A new job comes through in the end, and the two of them celebrate on the kitchen floor with a cheap bottle of fizz.
fails: The winter is long and cold between them, and something is left unsaid.
fails: {partner} snaps that pity is not love, and the house goes quiet for weeks.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- to build things that last (W U, cycle s1)

== the first wall laid true
tier: life event
aim: to build things that last
aim_role: spark
stages: juvenile young_adult adult mature
age: 15-65
per_year: 0 .3 .4 .4 .3 0
tone: joy
life: work, making
horizon: week
roles: mentor, boss, colleague, a neighbour
earth: a garden wall to build for a neighbour, the first job done without anyone's help
tribal: a stone fish-trap to build across the stream, the first done without an elder's help
magic: a footbridge to raise over the tower's moat, the first done without a master's help
scene: A neighbour wants a garden wall, and {mentor} has said {N} can do it alone this time. The bricks are stacked on the pavement and the string line is up.
scene W: {N} means to build it by the book: every course level, every joint filled.
scene U: {N} has worked out the footing depth, the frost line and the drainage, twice.
scene B: Do this well and the neighbour will tell the whole street who built it.
scene R: {N} wants the first course down by lunchtime, and to watch it rise.
scene G: The old wall that fell was made of stone from the field behind, and {N} wants the new one to belong.
- W | lay every course to the string line, and check each one with the level | v: conformity, achievement | dream: test | foot: mark learned a skill | chance: 70
- U | dig the footing twice as deep as the book says, for the frost | v: security | foot: lesson the hidden part holds the rest | chance: 72
- B | finish fast, take the money, and hand out cards up and down the road | v: achievement, power | foot: means money+.04 | chance: 80
- R | build it in one long day, radio on, without a break | v: stimulation | foot: means health-.03 | chance: 65
- G | reuse the old stones from the fallen wall, cleaned one by one | v: tradition, universalism | foot: person neighbour | chance: 68
- W>U | ask the old bricklayer down the road to check each course, and learn why | v: conformity, self-direction | dream: test | foot: person mentor | chance: 75
- U>B | price the job properly, every hour written down, before the first brick | v: achievement, security | foot: lesson time costs money too | chance: 78
- B>R | take on a second wall down the street before the first is done | v: achievement, stimulation | foot: means time-.06 | chance: 50
- R>G | let the neighbour's children press their hands into the last course of mortar | v: benevolence, stimulation | foot: means ties+.04 | chance: 85
- G>W | build it the old way, in lime mortar, so it can be mended for a century | v: tradition | foot: place prod.craft | chance: 60
works: The wall stands straight and true, and {mentor} runs a hand along the top and says nothing, which means a great deal.
works: The neighbour brings out tea and cake, and has already told three houses who built it.
fails: A course goes out of line halfway up, and the whole lot has to come down again.
fails: The first hard frost cracks the footing, and the neighbour wants the money back.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- to serve the public well (W U, cycle s4)

== the claim that went missing
tier: life event
aim: to serve the public well
aim_role: spark
stages: young_adult adult mature
age: 17-67
per_year: 0 0 .4 .4 .3 0
tone: mixed
life: work, public life
horizon: week
roles: boss, colleague, a family at the counter
earth: a family at the council counter whose housing claim has been lost in the system
tribal: a family at the store-keeper's fire whose share of the winter meat was never counted
magic: a family at the clerks' window whose grain-right was lost in the ledgers
scene: It is ten to five at the council counter, and a mother with two tired children says her housing claim was sent three months ago. The system says it never arrived.
scene W: Procedure says she must start again. {N} knows procedure, and knows where it fails.
scene U: Somewhere between the post room and the database a claim went missing, and {N} wants to know where.
scene B: {boss} likes a clean queue at five, and {N} likes {boss} to be pleased.
scene R: {N} cannot bear to send her away with a leaflet.
scene G: The children are asleep on the plastic chairs, and {N} thinks of {Ns} own family.
- W | open a new claim on the spot and mark it urgent, by the rules | v: conformity, benevolence | dream: test | foot: door helped someone in need | chance: 75
- U | stay after five and trace the lost claim through the post-room records | v: achievement, universalism | foot: means time-.04 | chance: 60
- B | ask her back on Monday, and shut the hatch on time | v: security | foot: door refused someone in need | chance: 90
- R | ring the housing director's own line and refuse to hang up | v: stimulation, benevolence | foot: mark defied an authority | chance: 45
- G | find the family a warm place for the weekend through the community hall | v: benevolence | foot: place gather.hall | chance: 70
- W>G | write up the gap in the system so that no other family falls through it | v: universalism | foot: place rule.counsel | chance: 55
- U>W | draw up a checklist for the counter, so every claim gets a receipt | v: security, conformity | dream: test | foot: lesson a receipt is a promise | chance: 72
- B>U | ask the clerk who knows the database to dig, and owe the favour | v: power, achievement | foot: person colleague | chance: 70
- R>B | threaten to go to the local paper unless the claim is found by Friday | v: power | foot: person rival | chance: 50
- G>R | give her a direct number, and promise to ring on Monday whatever happens | v: benevolence | foot: door kept your word | chance: 80
works: On Monday the claim turns up in a box in the basement, and the family is housed by the end of the month.
works: The mother comes back a week later just to shake {Ns} hand.
fails: The claim is never found, and the family goes to the back of a very long queue.
fails: {boss} calls {N} in for breaking procedure, and the family is no better off.

