earth: a friend at the kitchen table at midnight, with a choice they cannot make alone
tribal: a friend at the fire after dark, with a choice they cannot make alone
magic: a friend at the study door after the late bells, with a choice they cannot make alone
scene: It is nearly midnight, and {friend} is at {Ns} kitchen table, turning a mug round and round: take the job across the country, or stay?
scene W: {friend} came here because {N} always tells the truth, even the unwelcome kind.
scene U: {N} can see three questions hiding inside the one {friend} is asking.
scene B: If {friend} takes the job, {N} loses the best ally at work.
scene R: {N} wants to shout "go!" before {friend} has finished the sentence.
scene G: {friend} has roots here, a mother on the corner and an old dog, and {N} knows what roots weigh.
- W | ask the hard questions in turn, and leave the answer to them | v: benevolence, self-direction | dream: test | foot: door made a friend | chance: 70
- U | draw two columns on a napkin and work through every reason together | v: self-direction | dream: test | foot: lesson the question under the question | chance: 75
- B | steer them towards staying, for reasons of your own | v: power | foot: door hid a wrong | chance: 68
- R | tell them to go, now, before the fear wins | v: stimulation | foot: person friend lost | chance: 70
- G | make up the spare bed and say it will look clearer in the morning | v: benevolence | foot: mark helped someone in need | chance: 85
- W>B | say plainly what you would do in their place, and stand by it | v: conformity | foot: lesson honest words cost little | chance: 72
- U>R | look up the new city together that night, street by street | v: stimulation, self-direction | foot: means time-.03 | chance: 80
- B>G | remind them how much the family here leans on them, and let that weigh | v: tradition, power | foot: means ties+.03 | chance: 64
- R>W | promise to visit every month if they go, and mean it | v: benevolence | foot: door kept your word | chance: 70
- G>U | say nothing for a long while, and just listen until they hear themselves | v: benevolence | foot: means ties+.05 | chance: 78
works: {friend} decides by morning, and rings a year later to say it was the right call, and to thank {N} for it.
works: Word gets round that {N} is good to talk to, and the kitchen table sees a lot of midnights after that.
fails: {friend} takes the advice, it goes badly, and for a while {N} is the one who gets the blame.
fails: {friend} leaves with the question still open, and {N} lies awake wondering what else could have been said.

