- W>R | end on a toast, and a promise to hold this party again at a hundred | v: tradition, stimulation | foot: door kept your word | chance: 75
- U>G | have the old photographs framed and hung round the hall before anyone arrives | v: tradition | foot: means money-.03 | chance: 80
- B>W | ask the mayor to say a few words after, so the town sees the family's standing | v: power, conformity | dream: seal | foot: person patron | chance: 60
- R>U | make up a quiz on the family's history and set the young cousins against each other | v: stimulation | foot: lesson laughter keeps names alive | chance: 74
